Package: OncoSeq
Type: Package
Title: End-to-End Analysis of Cancer Transcriptomes and Genomes
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Umar", family = "Ahmad",
    email = "babasaraki@yahoo.co.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3216-5171"))
Description: OncoSeq provides a unified, end-to-end workflow for cancer
    transcriptomic and genomic data analysis. A single container class
    couples bulk RNA-sequencing counts with somatic mutation calls,
    gene-level copy-number alterations and clinical follow-up for the same
    set of tumour samples. The package covers data import from the Genomic
    Data Commons, cBioPortal and local quantification files; quality
    control and filtering; normalisation; differential expression through
    DESeq2, edgeR or limma-voom behind one interface; gene-set enrichment
    and over-representation testing; Kaplan-Meier and Cox survival
    modelling including genome-wide survival screens; mutation and
    copy-number summarisation; integration of genomic alterations with
    expression; and publication-ready visualisation. Every analysis is
    recorded in the object so that a complete study can be reproduced
    from one object.
